  {
    date: 'Oct 7, 2026',
    iso: '2026-10-07',
    material: true,
    summary: 'Fixed free tools that put what you typed into page addresses analytics recorded. Also: a homepage that leads with learning, starting routes you can follow, lessons that show where you are and end with what you now understand, a simpler one-currency net worth view, Frankfurter named in the notice, and OpenAI\'s training crawler blocked.',
    details: [
      'Internal visits: the team\'s own browsers can be marked so they are never counted. Opening any page with ?internal=1 sets a new key in your browser, nidhi-internal, and from then on that browser runs no analytics at all, not even anonymous pageviews; ?internal=0 removes it. The parameter is taken out of the address right away. Visitors who never open such a link see no change.',
      'Cookie settings: a "Cookie settings" link at the bottom of every page reopens the cookie banner, so you can change your answer as easily as you gave it. Before, a choice could only be undone by clearing your browser\'s site data. Choosing "No thanks" there after an earlier yes switches click recording off immediately, not just from your next visit. The choice is still stored only in your browser (nidhi-cookie-consent), and the link\'s own click is recorded only if you had accepted (data-attr footer-cookie-settings).',
      'Analytics paused, then a fresh start: from today until 00:00 UTC on October 8, 2026, the site records no analytics at all, and the newsletter sends no events either. From then on, analytics go to a new, empty PostHog Cloud EU project, under the same rules described above. The previous PostHog project, holding everything recorded before today, is being deleted.',
      'Free tools, what went wrong: the loan comparison (since it launched on May 10, 2026) and the net worth calculator (since May 17, 2026) wrote what you typed into the page address as you typed, so the page could be reloaded or bookmarked. Every page sends an anonymous pageview and page-leave event, and those carry the page address. So the amounts, rates, names and currencies you entered on those two tools reached our analytics (PostHog Cloud EU) inside that address, and so did the contents of any shared link opened to one of them. A link to any of the three tools with values after a ? would have been recorded the same way. The events carried no name, email or user ID, but this broke our promise that the values you type are never sent.',
      'Beliefs and the learning path: the principle behind every lesson is now said where people meet the site. The beliefs page has a new belief, "Not just the rules of thumb": a rule of thumb is a starting point, and each lesson explains why it exists, where it breaks and what depends on you. The learning path introduction says the same in one sentence. Wording only.',
      'Footer disclaimer: "nidhi offers guidance" and "Our suggestions are educational" read like advice, which the rest of the site is careful not to give. It now says nidhi provides educational information and tools, and that the content and tools are educational, not professional financial, investment or tax advice. Wording only.',
      'Homepage FAQ, "What happens to the numbers I type into the tools?": it said the numbers are not sent "to nidhi or anyone else". That was broader than precise. It now says they stay on your device and are not sent to nidhi, never go into the page address, and that when a tool needs outside data such as exchange rates, your browser asks that service for the rates only, never your amounts, which like any request shows it your IP address. Nothing changed in what is sent.',
      'Phones: no page scrolls sideways any more. Wide lesson tables scroll inside their own box (a small script wraps each table in a labelled, keyboard-focusable region as the page loads; it reads and stores nothing), the loan comparison\'s screen-reader data tables no longer widen the page, lesson text has the same side margin as its title, breadcrumbs on the tools and topics pages are at least 24 pixels tall, and topic card lesson counts are at least 12 pixels. Spaces that went missing next to links on the about, editorial policy, free tools, privacy and subscription-confirmed pages are back. Layout and wording only.',
      'Net worth calculator on phones: in the Share window, the Cancel and Copy link buttons sat half under the recipient preview, so a tap on their lower half missed. They now sit above it. Layout only.',
      'Free tools, what changed: no tool writes your inputs into the page address any more. A share link carries them after the # sign, a part of the address browsers never send to a server, and the page moves them out of the address bar before analytics start, so the pageview never sees them. Older links that carried the values after a ? still open, and are cleaned the same way. As a backstop, the analytics script now removes everything except campaign parameters (utm_source and the like) from any free-tool address before an event is sent. The section on what we collect now says this. One consequence: reloading a tool page no longer keeps what you typed; a share link keeps a copy. The events already recorded with these addresses are being deleted from PostHog.',
      'Lessons: every lesson and Inclusive Finances guide now ends with a short "What you now understand" list restating its main ideas, in a tinted box that mirrors the TL;DR at the top, before the free tool and the previous and next links.',
      'Homepage, for readers who already know the basics: a line under the hero buttons links straight to the Building and Psychology levels and to the free tools (data-attr labels home-hero-skip-building, home-hero-skip-psychology and home-hero-skip-tools, captured only with consent, as before), each starting card says who its route suits, and a short section explains how lessons go past the rule of thumb. No change to what data is collected.',
      'Lessons: each lesson in Discovery, Building, Psychology, Optimizing and Mastery says where it sits in its level (for example "Lesson 8 of 16") at the top and above the previous and next links, with a link to that level on the learning path. That link is at least 24 pixels tall, the minimum size for a tap target. The numbers come from the published lessons when the site is built; nothing about your reading is used.',
      'Lessons: those with a paired free tool end in a short path: the lesson you read, the idea in one line, and a link to the tool. Two more lessons now link to the net worth calculator: What Is Net Worth and Managing Money Across Currencies.',
      'Homepage, "Start wherever you are": each situation shows its lessons as a numbered route, names the free tools that go with it, and ends in one button into the route. If you have read lessons on that route, the button moves to the first one you have not read, and once you have read them all it points to the learning path. It reads the existing nidhi-reading-progress key in your browser to do this. Nothing is sent to us or anyone else, and no new key is stored.',
      'Homepage: numbered lessons keep their titles beside their numbers, "nidhi grows with your financial life" has more space between stages, and on phones the example chart is drawn narrower so its labels stay readable. Its footnote, and the description of the chart for screen readers, are now printed once in the page, not once per drawing. Small labels are at least 12 pixels, and the "Free Tools" menu button in the header is at least 24 pixels tall, the minimum size for a tap target.',
      'Homepage redesign: the page now leads with the free lessons and tools: where to start for your situation, which lesson goes with which tool, and how nidhi keeps up as finances get more complex. The planner and its early-access list come after them. The early-access form in the hero is gone; the one further down is the same form, sending and storing exactly what it did before. A short FAQ on the homepage is also published as structured data for search engines.',
      'Homepage example: the look-ahead step now grows an invested balance (€3,400 invested, €150 added a month, an illustrative 5% a year after inflation) instead of the whole net worth, because a net worth made of a car, cash, a pension and a loan does not grow at one rate. Its note now counts the starting €3,400 as money put in alongside the €18,000 added. Editorial only; nothing is collected or sent.',
